==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|fi|lang1=urj-fin-pro|*louna|as}}, from {{der|fi|urj-fpr-pro|*lowna||day, midday}}. Cognates include {{cog|krl|lounat||evening/main meal}}, {{cog|vep|louna}}, {{cog|vot|lõunõd||south, lunch}}, {{cog|et|lõuna||south, lunch}} and {{cog|koi|лун}}. Permic cognates have the meaning "day", whereas Baltic-Finnic cognates denote the direction where the Sun is at midday or the meal eaten at midday.

The compass point meaning was clarified in the 19th century and inverted compared to Estonian: southwest is ''lounas'' in Finnish and ''edel'' in Estonian while south is ''etelä'' in Finnish and ''lõuna'' in Estonian. In earlier text and dialects ''lounas'' may mean either south, southwest or southeast. Compare {{m|fi|lounatuuli||southern wind}}.<ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

